      {
        "id": "0b99111e65eb4d9faae97028d6140ff5-knowledge-0",
        "ref": null,
        "kind": "behavior",
        "statement": "compactLogsWithTrailing returns without deleting when lastLogIdx <= trailingLogs and otherwise deletes up to maxLog = min(snapshotIndex, lastLogIdx - trailingLogs), so the leader's retained log begins above the snapshot index when lastLogIdx - trailingLogs >= snapshotIndex at snapshot time. That condition is necessary for the snapshot boundary to be compacted away but is not sufficient for a rejoining peer to stay unrepairable: in retained CheckRun 62f089bd843641099558ff8d8831ab29 the backlog case (TrailingLogs=2, SnapshotThreshold=5, a 15 ms-per-apply FSM, 60 uncommitted commands on the peer) satisfied it - successor_snapshot at index 4 with successor_store_first 5 and store_last 63 - yet rejoin_observe reported restores_before/early/late all 0 with the peer at applied index 64 and store 61..62. In the same receipt the TrailingLogs=0 case loops (peer applied index pinned at 4, last index 7, thousands of installs) and the (TrailingLogs=10, 20 post-snapshot entries) and (25, 20) cases converge with restores 0 at index 24.",
        "conditions": "Retained run: five bootstrapped nodes in one process, InmemTransport/InmemStore, two-sided partition of {leader, partner} from the other three peers, four cases differing in TrailingLogs, post-snapshot entries and FSM speed; frozen snapshot fd2d6988362c434e9fda87b87c5fb0df.",
        "source_ids": [
          "src-compact19",
          "src-repl19",
          "src-repl-snap19",
          "src-installsnap19",
          "src-lastindex19"
        ],
